          "content": {
            "size": 20740,
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "compression": 0,
            "text": "<!DOCTYPE HTML>\n<html>\n    <head>\n    \n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/public/assets/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css?v=51\" type=\"text/css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/public/themes/style_light.css?v=51\" type=\"text/css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/public/assets/font-awesome/css/font-awesome.min.css?v=51\" type=\"text/css\">\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/public/assets/jquery/dist/jquery.min.js?v=51\"></script>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/public/assets/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.min.js?v=51\"></script>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/library/textformat.js?v=51\"></script>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/library/dialog.js?v=51\"></script>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/library/js/userDebug.js?v=51\"></script>\n\n    <title>Message Center Help</title>\n\n    <style>\n        @media only screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n           [class*=\"col-\"] {\n           width: 100%;\n           text-align:left!important;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n    </head>\n    <body>\n        <div class=\"container oe-help-container\">\n            <div>\n                <center><h2><a name = 'entire_doc'>Messages, Reminders, Recalls</a></h2></center>\n            </div>\n            <div class= \"row\">\n                <p>The messaging center conveniently consolidates communications options in one place.\n\n                <p>It lets you send messages and dated reminders to staff members, add patient to the recall list and send SMS text messages to patients.\n\n                <p>The default messaging center is divided into three sections - Messages, Reminders and Recalls.\n\n                <p>Additional functionality including the ability to send SMS text messages, automated phone dialing, emails etc. can be accessed by enabling the optional MedEx Communication Service.\n\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a href=\"#messages\">Messages</a></li>\n                    <li><a href=\"#reminders\">Reminders</a></li>\n                    <li><a href=\"#recalls\">Recalls</a></li>\n                    <li><a href=\"#medex_communication_service\">MedEx Communication Service</a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class= \"row\" id=\"messages\">\n                <h4 class=\"oe-help-heading\">Messages<a href=\"#\"><i class=\"fa fa-arrow-circle-up oe-pull-away oe-help-redirect\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></h4>\n                <p>Lets you send messages to staff members about patient related matters.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\"  aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>It is a part of the medical record.</strong>\n\n                <p>Upon logging in to openEMR a small envelope icon is visible on the top right. It shows the number of pending messages and dated reminders.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm oe-no-float\"><i class=\"fa fa-envelope\"></i></button>\n\n                <p>You can click on the envelope icon to access the messaging center.\n\n                <p>Alternatively it can be accessed by clicking in the Messages menu item in the top navigation bar.\n\n                <p>The messaging center will open with the Messages tab activated and will display the logged in user`s messages as indicated by the caption My Messages.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\"  aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>For those with administrative privileges an icon is displayed next to the My Messages caption.</strong>\n\n                <p>Clicking on the icon next to the caption will display everyone`s messages and the caption will change to All Messages.\n\n                <p>By default Active Messages are displayed as indicated in the section below the Messages caption.\n\n                <p>Clicking on the Show All or Show Inactive buttons will show the appropriate messages.\n\n                <p><strong>CREATING A NEW MESSAGE :</strong>\n\n                <p>To create a new message click on the Add New button at the bottom.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-add btn-sm oe-no-float\">Add New</button>\n\n                <p>It will open the Create New Message section.\n\n                <p>Select the message type to more accurately reflect the type of message you are sending. You may choose to leave it as unassigned.\n\n                <p>The message status will be New as it a new message that is being created.\n\n                <p>Select a patient by clicking on the patient input box.\n\n                <p>It will bring up the Multi patient finder  popup.&nbsp;\n                <i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\"  aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>New to openEMR 5.0.2</strong>\n\n                <p>Clicking on either the Enter Name or Enter ID tab will bring up the search box which you can use to select a patient.\n\n                <p>Click on Add to List button to add to the bottom section.\n                <button class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm oe-no-float\">Add to list</button>\n\n                <p>You can add multiple patients to the list.\n\n                <p>Click OK to import these patients into the patient input box.\n\n                <p>Click the Clear button to clear the imported patient names and start afresh.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-undo btn-sm oe-no-float\">Clear</button>\n\n                <p>Use the Select User dropdown box to select the user(s) to whom the message will be sent.\n\n                <p>You can add multiple users by selecting them one at a time.\n\n                <p>Click the Clear button to start afresh.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-undo btn-sm oe-no-float\">Clear</button>\n\n                <p>Type the message and click Send Message .\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-send-msg btn-sm oe-no-float\">Send Message</button>\n\n                <p>A new message can thus be sent to a single or multiple users and/or can be about a single or multiple patients.\n\n                <p><strong>ADD TO EXISTING MESSAGE :</strong>\n\n                <p>All pending messages are displayed on the MY MESSAGES pane.\n\n                <p>You can sort the pending messages in ascending or descending order by clicking on the arrowhead in each cell of the table header.\n\n                <p>Clicking on the patient`s name will reveal the message.\n\n                <p>You can only add to the existing message and cannot edit previously entered data.\n\n                <p>You can change the type or leave it as it is.\n\n                <p>There are four message statuses - New, Forwarded, Read and Done.\n\n                <p>Changing the status to Done will remove the message from the active message list.\n\n                <p>Changing the status to Read would leave it as a read message in the active messages list of the current user.\n\n                <p>If the message is forwarded it will show up in the active messages list of the user to whom the message was forwarded and disappear from the current user`s active messages list.\n\n                <p>Changing the status to New will achieve the same result.\n\n                <p>If desired the current message can be printed.\n\n                <p>Clicking on the Delete button will delete the message.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-delete btn-sm oe-no-float\">Delete</button>\n            </div>\n            <div class= \"row\" id=\"reminders\">\n                <h4 class=\"oe-help-heading\">Reminders<a href=\"#\"><i class=\"fa fa-arrow-circle-up oe-pull-away oe-help-redirect\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></h4>\n                <p>Otherwise known as Dated Reminders are short messages of up to 160 characters.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\"  aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>Unlike a message sent in Messages the dated reminder is not a part of the medical record.</strong>\n\n                <p>It can be either linked to a patient or just be a message addressed to another user(s).\n\n                <p>There are three actions that are possible - Create a New Dated Reminder, Forward and Set as Completed.\n\n                <p><strong>CREATING A NEW DATED REMINDER :</strong>\n\n                <p>Clicking on the Create A Dated Reminder button will bring up the Send a Reminder popup.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-add btn-sm oe-no-float\">Create A Dated Reminder</button>\n\n                <p>The first section lets you either link this message to a patient if so desired..\n\n                <p>The second section lets you choose to whom you wish to send the message.\n\n                <p>You can click on the Select All button to choose all authorized users.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-save btn-sm oe-no-float\">Select All</button>\n\n                <p>If the checkbox is checked and the message is sent to multiple users then each user has to sign off on the message by clicking the Set As Completed Button for that message.\n\n                <p>A due date can be specified or a specific time period can be chosen for the dated reminder to to show up.\n\n                <p>Set the priority level.\n\n                <p>Type a brief message and hit Send Message .\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-send-msg btn-sm oe-no-float\">Send Message</button>\n\n                <p>The messages that were sent by the user on that day will be displayed in the table below.\n\n                <p>The dated reminder will start to appear 5 days before the reminder date under Dated Reminders .\n\n                <p>The upcoming reminders have a green exclamation icon.&nbsp;\n                <i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-green\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p>The reminder for the current day will have an orange exclamation icon.\n                <i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\"  aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p>The reminders that are past the due date will have a red exclamation triangle icon.\n                <i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-triangle oe-text-red\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p>By default only five dated reminders are shown at a time.\n\n                <p>Increase the limit to a larger number say 100 so that you can decide on which ones to act upon.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-triangle oe-text-red\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>You need administrator privileges to increase the number of reminders to show.</strong>\n\n                <p>Go to Administration &gt; Globals &gt; CDR &gt; Dated reminders maximum alerts to show and change the value to a higher number.\n\n                <p>A dated reminder message can be either forwarded by clicking the Forward button or removed from the dated reminders list by clicking on the Set As Completed button.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-send-msg btn-sm oe-no-float\">Forward</button>\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-save btn-sm oe-no-float\">Set As Completed</button>\n\n                <p><strong>FORWARD A DATED REMINDER :</strong>\n\n                <p>The process for forwarding the message is quite similar to that of creating a new message.\n\n                <p>While forwarding a dated reminder the old message is displayed, it can be overwritten.\n\n                <p>The previous message can however be viewed by clicking on the View Log button.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-save btn-show btn-sm oe-no-float\">View Log</button>\n\n                <p>Clicking on the View Log button will bring up the Dated Message Log popup.\n\n                <p>Lets you filter the results as per the chosen criteria.\n\n                <p>If you hit the refresh button without setting any filters then all dated reminders for the user will appear below.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-refresh oe-no-float\">Refresh</button>\n\n                <p>The log table will show a list of both messages and dated reminders if any.\n\n                <p>The display window can be resized by clicking and dragging the bottom right corner of the window.\n\n                <p>Clicking on the slashed eye icon will hide the filters.\n                <i class=\"fa fa-eye-slash text-warning\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p>To reveal the filters click on the eye icon.\n                <i class=\"fa fa-eye text-warning\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p><strong>SET AS COMPLETED :</strong>\n\n                <p>Clicking on Set As Completed will remove the reminder from the active display.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-save btn-sm oe-no-float\">Set As Completed</button>\n            </div>\n            <div class= \"row\" id=\"recalls\">\n                <h4 class=\"oe-help-heading\">Recalls<a href=\"#\"><i class=\"fa fa-arrow-circle-up oe-pull-away oe-help-redirect\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></h4>\n                <p>This feature is used to add patients to a recall list, i.e those that need an appointment at a future date but the appointment has not yet been scheduled.\n\n                <p>Once an appointment is scheduled the name automatically drops off the recall board.\n\n                <p>The Recalls tab has two buttons New Recall and Recall Board.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-add oe-no-float\">New Recall</button>\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-transmit oe-no-float\">Recall Board</button>\n\n                <p><strong>ADD A NEW RECALL :</strong>\n\n                <p>Click on the New Recall button to open a new recall scheduling page.\n\n                <p>It contains a left and right section.\n\n                <p>Click on the Name text box on the left section to bring up the patient finder pop-up.\n\n                <p>Search and select a patient and click OK.\n\n                <p>If the patient has any demographic data entered in openEMR it will automatically populate the relevant fields on the right sections.\n\n                <p>Fill in any missing details or edit existing information. This will be saved in the patient`s demographics page in openEMR.\n\n                <p>The last visit date will automatically be filled.\n\n                <p>If the patient is being added to the recall list on the day of the visit it would reflect the current date.\n\n                <p>If the patient is calling back to be added to the list the last visit may be in the remote past. Be aware that the 1,2,3 plus years are calculated and displayed on the Date box at the bottom of this section.\n\n                <p>You could manually edit this date should you choose to or an entirely different date.\n\n                <p>Fill in the reason and select a provider and clinic and click the Add Recall button to complete the process.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-add oe-no-float\">Add Recall</button>\n\n                <p><strong>RECALL BOARD - Default - without MedEx Communication Service :</strong>\n\n                <p>This fully functional Recall Board included in the default install can be used to add patients to the recall list.\n\n                <p>To access it click on the Recall Board menu item in the top navigation bar or click on the Recall Board button in the Message Center.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-transmit oe-no-float\">Recall Board</button>\n\n                <p>The top portion of the Recall Board allows the setting of filters to display specified data.\n\n                <p>Enter or select the options in the various boxes to filter the results according to need and press Filter.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-filter oe-no-float\">Filter</button>\n\n                <p>The filtered results will show up in the section below it.\n\n                <p>The filter section can be hidden or revealed by clicking the arrowhead  on the bottom right .\n                <span class=\"text-right fa-stack fa-lg pull_right small oe-text-black\"style=\"position:relative;right:0;top:0;\">\n                    <i class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></i>\n                    <i id=\"print_caret\" class=\"fa fa-caret-up fa-stack-1x\"></i>\n                </span>\n\n                <p>The Name cell contains the name, date of birth, patient ID and date of last visit.\n\n                <p>You can click on the patient name to quickly access the patient`s chart.\n\n                <p>The Recall cell has the date of recall and the reason for recall.\n\n                <p>The Contacts cell has various bits of contact information like phone numbers, email etc.\n\n                <p>The next three cells are the action cells that let you perform some recall activity.\n\n                <p>If you check the check box in any of these cells it will generate an entry in the last cell called Progress.\n\n                <p>Checking the Postcards check box will let you print a postcard that can be mailed to a patient.\n\n                <p>Labels can be printed either for one patient or for all the selected patients.\n\n                <p>The Office: Phone cell lets you indicate a phone call was made.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>\n                The default installation will not make the phone call automatically.</strong>\n\n                <p>An appointment can be scheduled by clicking on the calendar icon in that cell.\n                <i class=\"fa fa-calendar-check-o fa-fw oe-text-black\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>\n\n                <p>Once an appointment is scheduled the recall will drop off the Recall Board.\n\n                <p>The Notes cell lets you add a note to an action that you take in the 3 action cells or just a note without any association to the action.\n\n                <p>The Progress cell lists all the actions along with any associated notes if any.\n\n                <p>You can delete the recall by clicking on the X button on the top right corner of the cell.\n\n                <p>If so desired the default board can be disabled by going to Administration &gt; Calendar &gt; Recall Board: Disable and checking the checkbox and click Save.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-triangle oe-text-red\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>You need administrator privileges to disable the default Recall Board.</strong>\n            </div>\n            <div class= \"row\" id=\"medex_communication_service\">\n                <h4 class=\"oe-help-heading\">MedEx Communication Service<a href=\"#\"><i class=\"fa fa-arrow-circle-up oe-pull-away oe-help-redirect\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a></h4>\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-circle oe-text-orange\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>It is a commercial messaging module available to openEMR practices utilizing version 5.0.1 and higher.</strong>\n\n                <p>MedEx automates Appointment Reminders and Recalls using phone calls, text messages and e-mails.\n\n                <p>Replies from patients are displayed directly in your EHR.\n\n                <p><i class=\"fa fa-exclamation-triangle  oe-text-red\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <strong>You need administrator privileges to enable the MedEx Communication Service.</strong>\n\n                <p>Go to Administration &gt; Globals &gt; Connectors and check the Enable MedEx Communication Service check box and click Save.\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-default btn-sm btn-save oe-no-float\">Save</button>\n\n                <p>Refresh the Message Center or just reopen it.\n\n                <p>A new tab sub menu will be visible at the top of the Message center page.\n\n                <p>Click on the File menu item on the top left of the Message center page ansd select Setup MedEx.\n\n                <p>It will take you to the MedEx sign-up page.\n\n                <p>More information available at the openEMR MedEx wiki page.\n                <a href=\"https://www.open-emr.org/wiki/index.php/MedEx\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><i class=\"fa fa-external-link text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-original-title=\"\" title=\"\"></i></a>\n\n                <p>The features of a MedEx enabled installation are explained in this video.\n                <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4lbJCpfotAo\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><i class=\"fa fa-video-camera text-primary\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-original-title=\"\" title=\"\"></i></a>\n\n                <p>SMS zone - This section lets use send and receive SMS texts.\n\n                <p>It is also a subscription based service.\n            </div>\n        </div><!--end of container div-->\n    </body>\n</html>\n"
          },
          "headersSize": 411,
          "bodySize": 20769,
          "redirectURL": "",
          "_transferSize": 21180
        },
